WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
Let’s talk about Israel’s new friends.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.920
For years many Arab countries banded together against Israel.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.280
But some countries are rethinking that.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:15.360
Some are even making it official.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.880
Some are even making it official.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:34.600
What they’re calling normalisation appears

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.280
to have been happening, quietly, for years.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.120
Now it’s out in the open

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.800
and the US is pretty much leading the whole thing.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.480
So what does normalisation even mean?

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.360
What’s in it for these countries?

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.600
And how does it affect the Palestinians?

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.960
Normalisation is basically diplomatic-speak 

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.000
for two countries having some kind of formal relationship

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.640
where before there was none

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.720
through things like trade deals, setting up embassies

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:07.920
and direct flights.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.720
But not that long ago the idea of Gulf countries

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.000
having cordial relations with Israel was unthinkable.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.600
There’s been a lot of bad blood.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:21.840
In 1948 Israel expelled around 750,000 Palestinians 

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.520
and declared itself a state.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.600
That basically sparked decades of on-again, off-again Arab-Israeli wars.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:32.640
At one point Saudi Arabia even sent in troops.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.560
At one point Saudi Arabia even sent in troops.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:41.320
Since then the problem has been how Israel is slowly

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:45.000
taking over Palestinian land by illegally building settlements

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.560
blockading the Gaza Strip

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.200
and militarily occupying everything else. 

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.400
So for as long as many can remember

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.160
Saudi Arabia has stood by the Palestinians

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.040
particularly King Salman.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.760
Together with other Arab states

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.760
the Saudis drew a line in the sand in 2002.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.280
But King Salman is not really in charge anymore.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.040
And his son seems to have other ideas.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.840
It’s why those recent reports of a secret Saudi-Israeli

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.040
meeting got so much attention.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.760
US and Israeli media say the American secretary of state

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.240
Mike Pompeo, was on an official visit to Saudi Arabia

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.800
when Benjamin Netanyahu flew over too.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.120
The Saudis, though, say it never happened. 

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.360
Other countries are already embracing a new friendship.

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:23.280
Bahrain and the United Arab Emirates both signed deals with Israel in 2020. 

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.000
Sudan has a normalisation agreement too.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:40.640
So why the change?

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.760
So where does all of this leave the Palestinians?

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:48.040
Well it weakens their leaders’ position to negotiate a peace deal with Israel

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.000
and for many Palestinian people it’ll just be harder

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:55.320
to get justice or undo decades of Israeli occupation.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.760
So why the change?

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:15.280
There was a UAE-Israeli trade conference

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.920
and Twitter pages are now promoting Israeli products

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.880
in the Gulf and Emirati products in Israel.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:32.400
Any other year this joint music video by Israeli and Emirati

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.720
artists would’ve just seemed weird.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.520
But this is 2020.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:45.800
Trading with Israel would make business sense

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.320
for Saudi Arabia too. 

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.160
But normalising with Israel

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:51.520
is about more than making money.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.240
It’s no secret that MBS is trying to remake

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.720
his own image as a modern leader.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:58.120
He’s got a lot to overcome.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.520
Think the war in Yemen

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.160
arresting critics

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.480
even accusations he was involved in the shocking

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:12.160
dismemberment of the journalist Jamal Khashoggi.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.280
So for a smooth ascension to the throne

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.840
MBS needs friends in high places.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:32.040
Back in 2018 Trump and MBS

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.000
were laughing it up in the Oval Office.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.920
The occasion was a business tour by Saudi Arabia. 

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.960
Under Trump it’s a relationship that seems to be able

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.080
to withstand just about anything.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.640
Even after Khashoggi’s murder Trump’s son-in-law

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.560
and adviser Jared Kushner kept in touch with MBS.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.280
But with Joe Biden as US president

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:00.080
that relationship is expected to change.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.120
But there’s still time for Trump and others

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:15.000
to influence the next four years.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.200
Especially when it comes to Iran.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:20.960
Because nothing makes friends quite like having a common enemy.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:36.520
One of the first things Trump did in office was pull out

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:40.160
of the nuclear deal and order more sanctions on Iran.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.160
But the incoming US president says

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:44.000
he wants to revive that deal. 

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.880
That could be why Trump seems to be pushing

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:49.880
all these new alliances in the Middle East before Biden gets in.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:01.680
A deal between MBS and Netanyahu won’t be 

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:04.000
an easy sell to many people in the region.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.680
There’s already been some resistance

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:07.680
to the deals that were signed before.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.600
Normalising ties with Israel’s Arab neighbours

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.720
is a big win for Netanyahu.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:17.240
Saudi Arabia would be the top prize.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.360
For all of them it’s good for business.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:22.080
For some it means isolating Iran. 

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.560
But for the Palestinians — it’s a betrayal.

